  "event_seq": 280,
  "root_problem": "Dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1220/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-07). Billing import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 and comparing raw AMI register values to 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling (E-13), misreads v4.2-firmware meters that report register values in 0.1 m3 units (E-14) as high-consumption, causing billing import to reject an otherwise validly-delivered AMI read (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION) and substitute an ESTIMATED bill instead; this accounts for 1184 of the 1240 ESTIMATED-type disputed bills (E-12). This confirmed mechanism explains the ESTIMATED-read share of disputes (41% of 3025, E-02) but does not yet explain the majority of disputes that carry ACTUAL read type (1785 of 3025, E-02), whose cause remains open."
 },
